💡 **IMPORTANT: pin the new wiring with a guard test — this exact regression class is currently silent**

This PR fixes a failure whose symptom appeared days later in production (#301 stalled `BLOCKED`), not at lint/parse time: an empty or dropped stub input only produces a GitHub "unexpected input" warning (or a silent no-op), while `rule.ciWorkflow \|\| jobParams.ciWorkflow \|\| 'quality.yml'` in `smAgent.js` keeps matching the validate rules without dispatching.

The repo already guards this file's fragile couplings — `test/machine_kit/factory_stub_ref_test.dart` pins the factory SHA + secret set, `machine_sm_watchdog_test.dart` pins cron/dryRun/secrets — but nothing pins the CI-dispatch wiring added here, nor its cross-file contracts:

- `machine-sm.yml` → `ci-workflow: quality.yml` and `machine-merge.yml` → `ci_workflow: quality.yml` (note the different spellings: `factory-sm.yml` declares `ci-workflow`, `factory-merge.yml` declares `ci_workflow` — a typo on either side is silently dropped);
- `quality.yml` keeps `workflow_dispatch: {}` (the SM is its **only** trigger) and its `name: Quality` matches `machine-merge.yml`'s `workflows: ['Quality']` trigger;
- the stamped required checks `["agents-suite","static","gate"]` remain real job names in `quality.yml`.

A cheap addition to `test/machine_kit/machine_sm_watchdog_test.dart`:

```dart
test('SM/merge stubs wire the dispatch-only CI knob (dmtools-agents#575)', () {
  final sm = File('.github/workflows/machine-sm.yml').readAsStringSync();
  final merge = File('.github/workflows/machine-merge.yml').readAsStringSync();
  final quality = File('.github/workflows/quality.yml').readAsStringSync();
  expect(sm, contains('ci-workflow: quality.yml'),
      reason: 'empty/absent left approved PRs stalled BLOCKED (#301)');
  expect(merge, contains('ci_workflow: quality.yml')); // underscore: factory-merge
  expect(quality, contains('workflow_dispatch: {}'),
      reason: 'dispatch-only CI — the SM is the only trigger');
  expect(quality, contains('name: Quality'),
      reason: "machine-merge.yml's workflow_run trigger matches this name");
  for (final job in ['agents-suite', 'static', 'gate']) {
    expect(RegExp('^  $job:', multiLine: true), matches(quality),
        reason: 'validation-checks stamps "$job" — it must stay a real job');
  }
});
```

This turns the next silent regression of this class into a red test at pre-commit instead of a stalled release.

